<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  A Dog Said... Animal Prosthetics 2 (SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2, Workshop 3238353862).

  ADS 2 keeps three abstract RecipeDefs, ADS_Cat1 (medieval replacements), ADS_Cat2 (+ simple prosthetics) and
  ADS_Cat3 (+ bionics), each with a hand-curated <recipeUsers> list, and copies those lists onto the real
  surgery recipes in its own last patch (Patches/z_Category_Patches.xml). An animal absent from all three lists
  offers only amputation and euthanasia, so without this file ADS 2 is a silent no-op for the penguins.

  Both penguins go into Cat1 and Cat2 and not Cat3. The choice follows their vanilla counterparts in ADS 2's own
  list (1.6/Defs/AnimalCategories/Animal_Categories.xml, read 2026-10-14): the mod gives the king penguin a duck's
  voice and the emperor penguin a goose's, and Duck, Goose, Emu and Ostrich are all in Cat1 and Cat2 and in none
  of Cat3. The lists are not nested, so the two additions are listed explicitly.

  The guard is PatchOperationConditional on ADS_Cat1. Without ADS 2 the xpath selects nothing, no <nomatch> is
  declared, and the operation reports success without logging anything. It is NOT MayRequire: MayRequire on an
  <Operation> is read by nothing. Each branch of the predicate repeats @Name=, since [@Name="A" or "B"] is true
  for every RecipeDef in the document.

  About.xml declares <loadBefore>SamBucher.ADogSaidAnimalProsthetics2</loadBefore>: ADS 2 copies the lists once,
  at its own patch, so this patch has to run first or it writes into lists nobody reads any more.
-->
<Patch>

	<Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
		<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[@Name="ADS_Cat1"]</xpath>
		<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
			<xpath>/Defs/RecipeDef[
				@Name="ADS_Cat2" or
				@Name="ADS_Cat1"
			]/recipeUsers</xpath>
			<value>
				<li>king_penguin</li>
				<li>emperor_penguin</li>
			</value>
		</match>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
